# Line endings, settled in the repository rather than in each machine's git config.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `core.autocrlf=true` writes CRLF into the working tree on checkout, and
# every tool in this project writes LF -- Node, Python, the page generators, the editors. A file
# that is checked out and then PARTLY rewritten therefore ends up carrying both, line by line.
# Measured on 20 Oct 2026 before this file was added: 2,702 of the generated pages and every one
# of the battle-data CSVs were mixed, and only 76 source files were cleanly LF.
#
# Nothing is functionally broken by that -- browsers and Node do not care -- but a test that
# reads a source file and matches a literal containing a newline is, and one was: the picker
# suite's "it does so before it binds the search box" check failed for weeks on line endings
# alone while the site behaved correctly.
#
# `eol=lf` removes the conversion instead of arguing with it. Git stores LF, checks out LF on
# every platform, and the tools write LF, so there is nothing left to mix. It also OVERRIDES
# core.autocrlf, which is the point: a local git setting fixes one machine, and this holds for
# anything that clones the repository -- another desktop, a CI runner, the daily pipeline.
#
# Nothing here wants CRLF. The files are served to browsers by Cloudflare Pages and read by Node
# and Python; no Windows tool in this project needs it, and Notepad has read LF since 2018.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Bytes. Declared rather than left to the heuristic, so nothing can ever decide to translate one
# of them: a single byte changed in a sprite or the Companion's release zip is a broken file.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.pdf   binary
